    {
      "id": "434498abcde1-q1",
      "number": 1,
      "question": "In the given figure, ABCD is a cyclic quadrilateral whose side AB is a diameter of the circle through A, B, C and D. If &ang;ADC = 130&deg;, then find &ang;CAB.",
      "questionHtml": "<p>In the given figure, ABCD is a cyclic quadrilateral whose side AB is a diameter of the circle through A, B, C and D. If&nbsp;&ang;ADC = 130&deg;, then find&nbsp;&ang;CAB.</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/images/production/quesImages/qImage65eac00c5c18d5e93bdf036d.png\" />&nbsp;</p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "30&deg;",
          "html": "30&deg;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "130 &deg;",
          "html": "130<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "50 &deg;",
          "html": "50<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "40 &deg;",
          "html": "40<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Given :</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">In a cylic quadrilateral ABCD.</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&ang;ADC = 130&deg;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Concepts Used :</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">&bull; The sum of the opposite angles of a cyclic quadrilateral is supplementary i.e. 180&ordm;.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">&bull;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);\">The angle at the circumference in a semicircle is always&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">90&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Solution :</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/images/production/quesImages/qImage65eac00c5c18d5e93bdf036d.png\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">We know that :</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&ang;ADC + &ang;ABC =&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">180</span><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">&ordm;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">&there4;</span>&nbsp;&ang;ABC = 180&ordm; -&nbsp;130&deg;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; &ang;ABC = 50&deg;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">We also know that :</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&bull; &ang;ACB = 90&ordm;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Now in&nbsp;&Delta;ABC :</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Sum of all interior angles of a triangle =&nbsp;180&ordm;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&ang;ABC +&nbsp;&ang;ACB +&nbsp;&ang;CAB =&nbsp;180&ordm;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&ang;CAB + 50&ordm; + 90&ordm; =&nbsp;180&ordm;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&ang;CAB =&nbsp;180&ordm; -&nbsp;&nbsp;50&ordm; -&nbsp;90&ordm;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&ang;CAB = 40&ordm;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Hence the correct answer is&nbsp;<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">&quot;40&ordm;&quot;.</span></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "//cdn.testbook.com/images/production/quesImages/qImage65eac00c5c18d5e93bdf036d.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "434498abcde1-q2",
      "number": 2,
      "question": "A cyclic-quadrilateral ABCD is inscribed in a circle with AB as diameter and centre at O. The side BC and AD are extended to meet at the point P. If an equilateral triangle is drawn inside the cyclic quadrilateral with the base as CD and vertex opposite to the base is at point O, then find the &ang;APB.",
      "questionHtml": "A cyclic-quadrilateral ABCD is inscribed in a circle with AB as diameter and centre at O. The side BC and AD are extended to meet at the point P. If an equilateral triangle is drawn inside the cyclic quadrilateral with the base as CD and vertex opposite to the base is at point O, then find the&nbsp;&ang;APB.",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "30 ∘",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">30</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "90 ∘",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">90</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "10 ∘",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">10</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "60 ∘",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">60</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">A cyclic-quadrilateral ABCD is inscribed in a circle with AB as diameter and centre at O.</span>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">The side BC and AD are extended to meet at point P.</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">An equilateral triangle is drawn inside the cyclic quadrilateral with the base as CD and the vertex opposite to the base is at point O.</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\"><strong>Concept used:</strong></span></p>\n\n<p>The angle subtended by an arc at the centre is twice that of&nbsp;the angle subtended by it at any point on the&nbsp;remaining part of the circumference of&nbsp;the circle.</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Madhuri_Railway_01.06.2022_D8.png\" style=\"height: 138px; width: 139px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">The value of each angle in the case of an equilateral angle triangle is 60<sup>∘</sup>.</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">The angle subtended by the diameter of the circle at any point on the circumference is 90</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span><span style=\"\">.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Pranali_Railway_01.06.2022_D11.png\" style=\"height: 151px; width: 171px;\" /></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\"><strong>Calculation:</strong></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">According to the question, the required figure is:</span></p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Madhuri_Railway_01.06.2022_D6.png\" style=\"height: 262px; width: 206px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>Now, Join points B and D.</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Madhuri_Railway_01.06.2022_D7.png\" style=\"height: 264px; width: 206px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>The angle subtended by the diameter of the circle at any point on the circumference is 90<sup>∘</sup>.</p>\n\n<p>Therefore,&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&ang;ADB +&nbsp;&ang;BDP = 180<sup>∘</sup></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span style=\"\">90</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;+&nbsp;&ang;BDP = 180</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;&ang;BDP = 90<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">The angle subtended by an arc at the centre is twice that of&nbsp;the angle subtended by it at any point on the&nbsp;remaining part of the circumference of&nbsp;the circle.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">Therefore,</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;&ang;DOC = 2 &times; &ang;DBC</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; 60<sup>∘</sup>&nbsp;= 2 &times; &ang;DBC</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; &ang;DBC =&nbsp;<span style=\"\">&ang;DBP</span> = 3<span style=\"\">0</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span></p>\n\n<p>Now,&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>In&nbsp;&Delta;BDP,</p>\n\n<p>&ang;BDP +&nbsp;&ang;DBP +&nbsp;&ang;BPD =&nbsp;<span style=\"\">180</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span style=\"\">90</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<span style=\"\">3</span><span style=\"\">0</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>&nbsp;+&nbsp;&ang;BPD =&nbsp;180<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;120<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>&nbsp;+&nbsp;&ang;BPD =&nbsp;180<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span></p>\n\n<div>\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;&ang;BPD = 60<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>&there4; The value of the required angle is 60<sup>∘</sup>.</strong></p>\n</div>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Madhuri_Railway_01.06.2022_D8.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Pranali_Railway_01.06.2022_D11.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Madhuri_Railway_01.06.2022_D6.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Madhuri_Railway_01.06.2022_D7.png"
      ],
