    {
      "id": "434498abcde1-q3",
      "number": 3,
      "question": "IJKL is a cyclic quadrilateral. IJ is extended up to M and N on both sides. if the value of &ang;KJM is 72&deg; and &ang;LIN = 78 &deg; , then find the value of &ang;ILK + &ang;JKL.",
      "questionHtml": "<p>IJKL is a cyclic quadrilateral. IJ&nbsp;is extended up to M and N on both sides. if the value of &ang;KJM&nbsp;is 72&deg; and&nbsp;<span style=\"\">&ang;LIN</span>&nbsp;= 78<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>, then find the value of <span style=\"\">&ang;ILK</span>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<span style=\"\">&ang;JKL.</span></p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "120 &deg;",
          "html": "120<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "150 &deg;",
          "html": "150<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "160 &deg;",
          "html": "160<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "75 &deg;",
          "html": "75<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/09/F1_Vinanti_SSC_29.09.22_D1.png\" style=\"width: 239px; height: 134px;\" /></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">IJKL is a cyclic quadrilateral</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&nbsp;IJ&nbsp;is extended up to M and N on both sides</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&ang;KJM</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;=&nbsp;72&deg; ,&nbsp;</span><span style=\"\">&ang;LIN</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;= 78</span><span style=\"\">&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"\">Concept used:</span></strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">Sum of the opposite angles of a cyclic quadrilateral is 180</span><span style=\"\">&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p>As per the question,</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&ang;LIN</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;= 78&deg;, </span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">so,&nbsp; &ang;LIJ =&nbsp;&nbsp;180&deg; - 78&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr; 102&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">So,&nbsp;&ang;JKL = 180 - 102</span><span style=\"\">&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr; 78&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">Again,</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&ang;KJM</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;=&nbsp;72&deg;,</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">So,&nbsp;&ang;KJI&nbsp;= 180&deg;&nbsp;- 72&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr; 108&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">Now,</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&ang;ILK = 180&deg; -&nbsp;&nbsp;108&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;72&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">So,</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&ang;ILK&nbsp;+&nbsp;&ang;JKL =&nbsp;78&deg;+&nbsp;72&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;150&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"\">&there4; The sum of&nbsp;&ang;ILK and&nbsp;&ang;JKL is&nbsp;150&deg;</span></strong></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/09/F1_Vinanti_SSC_29.09.22_D1.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "434498abcde1-q4",
      "number": 4,
      "question": "In a cyclic quadrilateral ABCD, &ang;DCB = 60&deg;, the side length BC = 10 cm, CD = 30 cm and AD = 20 cm. DB is diagonal to the quadrilateral ABCD. If the area of triangle DAB is 60% of the area of the triangle DCB, then find the length of AB. (in cm)",
      "questionHtml": "In a cyclic quadrilateral ABCD, &ang;DCB = 60&deg;, the side length BC = 10 cm, CD = 30 cm and AD = 20 cm. DB is diagonal to the quadrilateral ABCD. If the area of triangle DAB is 60% of the area of the triangle DCB, then find the length of AB. (in cm)",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "20",
          "html": "20"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "9",
          "html": "9"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "3",
          "html": "3"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "15",
          "html": "15"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&ang;DCB = 60&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">BC = 10 cm</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">CD = 30&nbsp;cm</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">AD = 20 cm</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Concept used:</strong></p>\n\n<p>Area of a triangle = 1/2&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;sin&theta;&nbsp;&times; side<sub>1&nbsp;</sub>&times; side<sub>2</sub></p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/07/Trigo.png\" style=\"width: 392px; height: 218px;\" /></p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/07/image.png\" style=\"width: 482px; height: 216px;\" /></p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/11/F3_Savita_SSC_28-11-22_D14.png\" style=\"width: 181px; height: 185px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>Let AB be x</p>\n\n<p>Now,</p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\rm \\frac{\\frac{1}{2}× x ×20 × sin120^o}{\\frac{1}{2}× 30 ×10 × sin60^o} = \\frac{3}{5}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\rm \\frac{x ×2 × \\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}}{30 × \\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}} = \\frac{3}{5}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;</span>5x = 3&nbsp;&times; 15</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; x = 45/5</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; x = 9</p>\n\n<p>So, AB = 9 cm</p>\n\n<p><strong>&there4; T<span style=\"\">he length AB&nbsp;(in cm) is 9.</span></strong></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/07/Trigo.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/07/image.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/11/F3_Savita_SSC_28-11-22_D14.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "434498abcde1-q5",
      "number": 5,
      "question": "A quadrilateral ABCD is inscribed in a circle such that the &ang;ACD = 35 ∘ and base AB is diameter to the circle. Find &ang;DAB.",
      "questionHtml": "A quadrilateral ABCD is inscribed in a circle such that the&nbsp;&ang;ACD = 35<sup>∘</sup>&nbsp;and&nbsp;base AB is diameter to the circle. Find &ang;DAB.",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "55 ∘",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">55</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "15 ∘",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">15</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "45 ∘",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">45</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "90 ∘",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">90</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p style=\"\">The required image is, since the angle subtended by the diameter of the circle at any point on the circumference is 90<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>,</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Madhuri_Railways_15.06.2022_D2.png\" style=\" height: 170px; width: 186px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Therefore, ∠ACB = 90<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Now, ∠ DCB = ∠ACD + ∠ACB </p>\n\n<p style=\"\">⇒ ∠ DCB = 35<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span> + 90<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span> = <span style=\"\">125</span><span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Since the sum of the opposite angle to a quadrilateral is 180<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>,</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Hence,  ∠DAB = 180<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span> - <span style=\"\">∠DCB = 180</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span><span style=\"\"> - </span><span style=\"\">125</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span><span style=\"\"> = 55</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Madhuri_Railways_15.06.2022_D2.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "434498abcde1-q6",
      "number": 6,
      "question": "ABCD is a cyclic quadrilateral. AB and DC when produced, meet in E. Which of the following statements is/are correct? 1. &Delta;EBC is similar to &Delta; EAD. 2. &ang;CBE + &ang; DAE = 180&deg;. Select the correct answer using the code given below :",
      "questionHtml": "<p>ABCD is a cyclic quadrilateral. AB and DC when produced, meet in E. Which of the following statements is/are correct?</p>\n\n<p>1.&nbsp;&Delta;EBC is similar to <span style=\"\">&Delta;</span>EAD.</p>\n\n<p>2.&nbsp;&ang;CBE + <span style=\"\">&ang;</span>DAE = 180&deg;.</p>\n\n<p>Select the correct answer using the code given&nbsp;below :</p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Only 1",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">Only 1</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Only 2",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">Only 2</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Both 1 and 2",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">Both 1 and 2</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Neither 1 nor 2",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">Neither 1 nor 2</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Concept:</strong></p>\n\n<p><strong>Similar Triangle: </strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Both have the same shape but sizes may be different</li>\n\t<li>Each pair of corresponding angles are equal.</li>\n\t<li>The ratio of corresponding sides is the same.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cyclic Quadrilateral:&nbsp;</strong>A cyclic quadrilateral has opposite angles that sum 180 degrees, the total sum of the angles equals 360 degrees.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement I:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"\">&Delta;EBC is similar to&nbsp;</span><span style=\"\">&Delta;EAD.</span><br />\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/05/F1_Vinanti_Defence_23.05.23_D1.png\" style=\"width: 404px; height: 186px;\" /><br />\nIn&nbsp;△EBC and&nbsp;△EAD,&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;&ang;E =&nbsp;&ang;E&nbsp; &nbsp; [common]</p>\n\n<p>From the figure</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;&ang;EBC =&nbsp;&alpha;,&nbsp;&ang;EAD =&nbsp;&theta;&nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>So,&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">&ang;EBC &ne; &ang;EAD &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p>We know that Each pair of corresponding angles of a similar triangle should</p>\n\n<p>be&nbsp;equal.</p>\n\n<p>Therefore,</p>\n\n<p>But&nbsp;<span style=\"\">△EBC ~&nbsp;△EAD is not correct</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><b>Statement II:&nbsp;</b></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;&ang;CBE +&nbsp;&ang;DAE =&nbsp;&alpha; +&nbsp;&theta;&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p>We know that&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">&alpha; +&nbsp;&theta;&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;= 180&deg; will be possible if ABCD is square. In this case, line AB &amp; CD</p>\n\n<p>will not intersect at E.</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">&alpha; +&nbsp;&theta;&nbsp;&nbsp;&ne;&nbsp;180&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">Hence, Statement II is incorrect.</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>&there4; Both statement I &amp; II are incorrect.</strong></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/05/F1_Vinanti_Defence_23.05.23_D1.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "434498abcde1-q7",
      "number": 7,
      "question": "In a cyclic quadrilateral PQRS, if PQ ∥ RS and &ang;P = 85&deg; then &ang; Q =",
      "questionHtml": "In a cyclic quadrilateral PQRS, if PQ&nbsp;<span style=\"\">∥</span> RS and &ang;P = 85&deg; then <span style=\"\">&ang;</span>Q =",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "85 &deg;",
          "html": "85<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "95 &deg;",
          "html": "95<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "105 &deg;",
          "html": "105<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "75 &deg;",
          "html": "75<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/04/F2_Savita_Defence_10-4-23_D1.png\" style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); width: 108px; height: 102px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">In a cyclic quadrilateral PQRS.</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">∠P = 85°, The sum of opposite angles in a cyclic quadrilateral is 180°.</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">∠P + ∠R = 180°  ⇒ ∠R = 180° - ∠P ⇒ ∠R = 180° - 85° ⇒ ∠R = 95°</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Now, ∠Q = 180° - ∠R ⇒ ∠Q = 180° - 95°  ⇒ ∠Q = 85° </p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/04/F2_Savita_Defence_10-4-23_D1.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "434498abcde1-q8",
      "number": 8,
      "question": "In the given figure ABCD and ABEF are two cyclic quadrilaterals. If &ang;BCD = 110&deg; then find &ang;BEF.",
      "questionHtml": "<p>In the given figure ABCD and ABEF are two cyclic quadrilaterals. If&nbsp;&ang;BCD = 110&deg; then find&nbsp;&ang;BEF.</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/05/F1_Shashi_SSC_21.05.2022_D1.png\" style=\"height: 217px; width: 291px;\" /></p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "55&deg;",
          "html": "55&deg;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "70 &deg;",
          "html": "70<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "90 &deg;",
          "html": "90<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "110 &deg;",
          "html": "110<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&ang;BCD = 110&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Concept used:</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">The sum of a pair of opposite angles is 180&deg;(supplementary).</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Let &ang;A, &ang;B, &ang;C, and &ang;D be the four angles of an inscribed quadrilateral then</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&ang;A + &ang;C = 180&deg; and &ang;B + &ang;D = 180&deg;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/05/F1_Shashi_SSC_21.05.2022_D2.png\" style=\"height: 216px; width: 292px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>In the 1st circle, ABCD is a <span style=\"\">cyclic quadrilateral</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">According to the concept,</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&ang;BCD +&nbsp;&ang;BAD = 180&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr; 110&deg; +&nbsp;&ang;BAD = 180&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;&ang;BAD = 180&deg; - 110&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;&ang;BAD = 70&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">In the 2nd circle ABEF is&nbsp;a&nbsp;</span><span style=\"\">cyclic quadrilateral</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">So,</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&ang;BAF +&nbsp;&ang;BEF = 180&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr; 70&deg; +&nbsp;&ang;BEF&nbsp;= 180&deg;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;&ang;BEF = 180&deg; - 70&deg;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;&ang;BEF = 110&deg;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong>&there4;&nbsp;<span style=\"\">&ang;BEF is 110&deg;.</span></strong></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/05/F1_Shashi_SSC_21.05.2022_D1.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/05/F1_Shashi_SSC_21.05.2022_D2.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "434498abcde1-q9",
      "number": 9,
      "question": "The sides AB and DC of a cyclic quadrilateral ABCD are produced to meet at E and the sides AD and BC are produced to meet at F. If &ang;AFB = 52&deg; and &ang; FBE = 102 &deg; , then what is the measure of &ang; BEC?",
      "questionHtml": "The sides AB and DC of a cyclic quadrilateral ABCD are produced to meet at E and the sides AD and BC are produced to meet at F. If &ang;AFB = 52&deg; and <span style=\"\">&ang;</span>FBE = 102<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>, then what is the measure of <span style=\"\">&ang;</span>BEC?&nbsp;",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "26 &deg;",
          "html": "26<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "38 &deg;",
          "html": "38<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "28 &deg;",
          "html": "28<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "36 &deg;",
          "html": "36<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">The sides AB and DC of a cyclic quadrilateral ABCD are produced to meet at E and the sides AD and BC are produced to meet at F.</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&ang;AFB = 52&deg; and&nbsp;</span><span style=\"\">&ang;</span><span style=\"\">FBE = 102</span><span style=\"\">&deg;</span><span style=\"\">,</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Concept used:</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">In the case of a cyclic quadrilateral, the value of the interior angle is equal to the opposite exterior angle.</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">The sum of all internal angles of a triangle is 180<sup>∘</sup>.</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\"><strong>Calculation:</strong></span></p>\n\n<p>According to the question, the required figure is:</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/05/F7_Madhuri_Engineering_12.05.2022_D7.png\" style=\"height: 201px; width: 194px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>The value of the interior angle is equal to the opposite exterior angle.</p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;&ang; ADC =&nbsp;&ang; CBE = 102<sup>∘</sup></p>\n\n<p>The value of a straight angle is 180<sup>∘</sup>.</p>\n\n<p>&ang; ADC +&nbsp;&ang; CDF =&nbsp;<span style=\"\">180</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; <span style=\"\">102</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span> +&nbsp;&ang; CDF =&nbsp;180<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;&ang; CDF = 78<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>In&nbsp;&Delta;CDF,</p>\n\n<p>&ang; CDF&nbsp;+&nbsp;&ang; FCD +&nbsp;&ang; DFC = 180<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span style=\"\">78</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>&nbsp;+&nbsp;&ang; FCD + 52<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>&nbsp;= 180<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;&ang; FCD + 130<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>&nbsp;= 180<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;&ang; FCD&nbsp;= 50<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>As we know, vertically opposite angle are equal.</p>\n\n<p>So,</p>\n\n<p>&ang; BCE = &ang; FCD = 50<sup>∘</sup>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>In &Delta; BEC,</p>\n\n<p>&ang; BEC + &ang; BCE + &ang; EBC = 180<sup>∘</sup></p>\n\n<p>&rArr; &ang; BEC + 50<sup>∘</sup> + 102<sup>∘</sup> = 180<sup>∘</sup></p>\n\n<p>&rArr; &ang; BEC + 152<sup>∘</sup> = 180<sup>∘</sup></p>\n\n<p>&rArr; &ang; BEC = 28<sup>∘</sup></p>\n\n<p>&there4;<strong> The value of the required angle is&nbsp;<span style=\"\">28</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>.<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/05/F7_Madhuri_Engineering_12.05.2022_D7.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "434498abcde1-q10",
      "number": 10,
      "question": "In the given figure, AB is the diameter of the circle of length 97 cm. If AC = 65 cm, CD = 56 cm and &ang;D = 90 ∘ , then find the area of quadrilateral ABCD.(AD and DC are not the tangents to the circle.)",
      "questionHtml": "<p>In the given figure, AB is the diameter of the circle of length 97 cm. If AC = 65 cm, CD = 56 cm and&nbsp;&ang;D = 90<sup>∘</sup>, then find the area of quadrilateral ABCD.(AD and DC are not the tangents to the circle.)</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Madhuri_Railways_22.06.2022_D11.png\" style=\"height: 213px; width: 211px;\" /></p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "6464 cm 2",
          "html": "6464 cm<sup>2</sup>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "3284 cm 2",
          "html": "3284 cm<sup>2</sup>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "3264 cm 2",
          "html": "3264 cm<sup>2</sup>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "6431 cm 2",
          "html": "6431 cm<sup>2</sup>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p style=\"\"><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">The diameter of the circle AB =&nbsp;97 cm</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">AC = 65 cm, CD = 56 cm and&nbsp;&ang;D = 90</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span><span style=\"\">.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\"><strong>Concept used:</strong></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">(1) The angle subtended by the diameter of the circle at any point on the circumference is 90<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>.</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Pranali_Railway_01.06.2022_D11.png\" style=\"height: 151px; width: 171px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">(2)&nbsp;Pythagoras theorem:</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">H<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;= L<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;+ B<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">(3) Area of a right-angle&nbsp;triangle.</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">A =&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)</span>&nbsp;&times; L&nbsp;&times; B</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Where,</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F2_Madhuri_Railways_03.06.2022_D6.png\" style=\"height: 191px; width: 167px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">H, is the hypotenuse</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">L, is the perpendicular</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">B, is the base</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">According to the question, the required figure is:</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Madhuri_Railways_22.06.2022_D11.png\" style=\" height: 213px; width: 211px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Since&nbsp;&Delta;ADC is a right-angle triangle at D.</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Therefore, apply the Pythagoras theorem on&nbsp;<span style=\"\">&Delta;ADC.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">&rArr; AC<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;= AD<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;+ CD<sup>2</sup></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; 65<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;= AD<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;+ 56<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; 4225&nbsp;= AD<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;+ 3136</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; AD<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;= 1089</p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;AD&nbsp;= 33 cm</p>\n\n<p>The area of&nbsp;&Delta;ADC =&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)</span>&nbsp;&times; 56&nbsp;&times; 33 = 924 cm<sup>2</sup></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">As we know, the angle subtended by the diameter of the circle at any point on the circumference is 90</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span><span style=\"\">.</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">Therefore,&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&ang;ACB = 90<sup>∘&nbsp;</sup></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">In&nbsp;&Delta;ABC right-angle at C.</span></p>\n\n<p>Apply t<span style=\"\">he Pythagoras theorem on&nbsp;</span><span style=\"\">&Delta;ABC.</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr; AB<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;= AC<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;+ BC<sup>2</sup></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; 97<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;= 65<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;+ BC<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; 9409&nbsp;= 4225&nbsp;+ BC<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;BC<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;= 5184</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; BC&nbsp;= 72 cm</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">The area of&nbsp;&Delta;ABC&nbsp;=&nbsp;</span><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;&times; 72&nbsp;&times; 65&nbsp;= 2340&nbsp;cm</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">The total area of quadrilateral ABCD = Area of&nbsp;&Delta;ABC + Area of ADC</p>\n\n<p>The total area of quadrilateral ABCD = 924<span style=\"\">&nbsp;cm</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span><span style=\"\">+ 2340&nbsp;cm</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;= 3264 cm<sup>2</sup></p>\n\n<p><strong>&there4; The required answer is&nbsp;<span style=\"\">3264 cm</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span></strong>.</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span>Some important formulas&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>(1) The two angles opposite to the side of equal length are congruent.</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Pranali_Railway_01.06.2022_D5.png\" style=\"height: 175px; width: 205px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">If AB = AC, then&nbsp;&ang;ABC =&nbsp;&ang;ACB</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">(2) The sum of all internal angles for a triangle is 180<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span>.</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Madhuri_Railway_01.06.2022_D1.png\" style=\"height: 184px; width: 172px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700; \">Most frequently asked theorem in Exams.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">(1)&nbsp;Alternate segment theorem:</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Pranali_Railway_01.06.2022_D6.png\" style=\"height: 156px; width: 215px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">As per the above figure, the angle (&theta;) between a tangent and a chord is equal to the angle (&theta;) in the alternate segment.</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">(2) The sum of opposite angles in a cyclic quadrilateral = 180<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">∘</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Madhuri_Railways_22.06.2022_D10.png\" style=\"height: 234px; width: 186px;\" /></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Madhuri_Railways_22.06.2022_D11.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Pranali_Railway_01.06.2022_D11.png",
